Stack: (Array, Linked) LIFO (Last In First Out)
Push(), Pop(), Peak() are three basic commands for Stack
Push() will insert a value into a stack, before adjusting the stack
pointer
Pop() will remove a stack, deleting it's contents and making it empty

Stacks will be Pop() in reverse order, ascending from stack layers

Push() will always start from the head of a Linked List


Queue: (Array, Linked) FIFO (First In First Out)

DeQueue: Removing a value from queue

EnQueue: Appending value to queue

Double Linked List: Stack and Queue have a limited base of operations
A Double Linked List has another reference pointer that allows the Linked List to be
back tracked through

Double Linked List will be foundational for the Tree Data Structure, which
will traverse using two reference pointers as well (left and right)

